      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e I do kinda wonder if we should make ctx.Fatalf prepend the `FAILED:` message (if there isn\u0027t one already) so that more of these errors get parsed correctly.\n\nThis is exactly what I started doing but buildbot really expects \"FAILED:\" to be at the beginning of the line. In Fatalf(), we write the timestamp first, followed by the failure message (that is how the logger is configured). So if I were to add this to Fatalf(), then it would be something like:\n```\nerrMsg \u003d \"soong_ui failed\\nFAILED: \u003cactual error for which Fatalf() is being called for\u003e\"\n```\n\nThis didn\u0027t look clean either, so I opted to keep the hack enclosed to just the RBE error message.\n\n\u003e The abstraction here isn\u0027t great, as it would also be nice if failures also showed up in the error.log file, but that currently requires going through the status.ToolStatus which isn\u0027t as simple as I wish it was (`ctx.Status.StartTool().Error(fmt.Sprintf(...))`). Refactoring things so that Status is the provider of the log-like functionality to the majority of the users (you can\u0027t do it to the ones implementing Status without potentially causing loop issues) would probably be the best way to do that, but it\u0027s also a fairly invasive change.\n\nYeah I\u0027m not sure if I want to take up a larger refactoring ;)",
